  },
  data: {
    LLM: 'Blinds are posted. Each player receives five cards and a pre-flop betting round follows. Dealer burns one and deals three community cards (flop); second betting round. Each player may then discard zero to five cards and receive that many replacements from the deck. Dealer burns one and deals the turn card; third betting round. Dealer burns one and deals the river; fourth betting round. At showdown the pot is split between the best five-card hand (private cards only) and the best Omaha hand (exactly two hole cards plus exactly three board cards).',
    Player: 'Blinds are posted. Each player receives five cards and a pre-flop betting round follows. Dealer burns one and deals three community cards (flop); second betting round. Each player may then discard zero to five cards and receive that many replacements from the deck. Dealer burns one and deals the turn card; third betting round. Dealer burns one and deals the river; fourth betting round. At showdown the pot is split between the best five-card hand (private cards only) and the best Omaha hand (exactly two hole cards plus exactly three board cards).',
    objective: 'Win chips by having the best five-card hand (from your five private cards) and the best Omaha hand (two of your cards plus three board cards) at showdown; the pot is split between these two halves.',
    gameplay: 'Blinds are posted. Each player receives five cards and a pre-flop betting round follows. Dealer burns one and deals three community cards (flop); second betting round. Each player may then discard zero to five cards and receive that many replacements from the deck. Dealer burns one and deals the turn card; third betting round. Dealer burns one and deals the river; fourth betting round. At showdown the pot is split between the best five-card hand (private cards only) and the best Omaha hand (exactly two hole cards plus exactly three board cards).',
    keyRules: [
      "Pot limit betting. Blinds and order as in Texas Hold'em and Omaha.",
      'After the flop betting round, each player may discard 0-5 cards and receive an equal number of replacements.',
      'Pot splits between best five-card hand (all five in hand) and best Omaha hand (two from hand, three from board).',
      'Standard poker hand rankings for both halves. One player can scoop the entire pot by winning both halves.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Five to seven players; optimum is 5 or 6. Up to 9 can play but the deck may need recycling from the muck for replacements.',
      deck: 'Standard international 52-card deck (four suits, Ace through King).',
      equipment: 'Standard international 52-card deck (four suits, Ace through King).',
      dealing: 'Deal 5 cards each. Small Blind/Big Blind.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'Blinds are posted. Each player receives five cards and a pre-flop betting round follows. Dealer burns one and deals three community cards (flop); second betting round. Each player may then discard zero to five cards and receive that many replacements from the deck. Dealer burns one and deals the turn card; third betting round. Dealer burns one and deals the river; fourth betting round. At showdown the pot is split between the best five-card hand (private cards only) and the best Omaha hand (exactly two hole cards plus exactly three board cards).',
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Base game uses blinds only; ante appears only in Communist Pot variation.',
