    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Win chips by having the best five-card hand (from your five private cards) and the best Omaha hand (two of your cards plus three board cards) at showdown; the pot is split between these two halves.',
      'Turn-flow example: Blinds are posted. Each player receives five cards and a pre-flop betting round follows. Dealer burns one and deals three community cards (flop); second betting round. Each player may then discard zero to five cards and receive that many replacements from the deck. Dealer burns one and deals the turn card; third betting round. Dealer burns one and deals the river; fourth betting round. At showdown the pot is split between the best five-card hand (private cards only) and the best Omaha hand (exactly two hole cards plus exactly three board cards).',
      "Scoring example: Pot is split between the best five-card hand (using only the player's five private cards) and the best Omaha hand (exactly two hole cards plus exactly three board cards). Same player can scoop both halves. Win one or both halves of the pot at showdown: best five-card hand and best Omaha hand (two from hand, three from board). Standard poker hand rankings for both..",
